[2026-07-07 19:04Z] source=strategy-advisor(sonnet5,deep) · topic=try-catch-confirm
OBSERVATION: Re-verified tick-1 finding (chat.mjs runTurn has no try/catch) one level
deeper by tracing the full unwind path. bin/tmct.mjs:447-449 DOES have a top-level
`main().catch((e) => { stderr write; process.exit(1); })`, but it does not neutralize
the bug — it only prevents an ugly unhandled-rejection stack dump while still killing
the whole process. Confirmed exact mechanics: src/chat.mjs:2462 `await runTurn(...)`
inside session.turn() (no try/catch) throws before writeLog/writeSidecar/turns+=1
execute for that turn, so the failing turn is silently dropped from both artifacts.
Worse: the exception propagates past the for-await loop in runChat (chat.mjs:2525-2536)
without reaching `rl.close()` (2536) or `await session.close()` (2538) — session.close()
is the ONLY call that writes end-markers AND flushes the log/sidecar write streams
(`stream.end()`/`sidecar.end()`, chat.mjs:2489-2490). Since close() is skipped entirely,
process.exit(1) at bin/tmct.mjs:449 can fire before Node flushes the still-open
write streams to disk — a real durability risk beyond "session aborts," the tail of
the log/sidecar can be lost, not just truncated cleanly.
RECOMMENDED ACTION: Confirmed real, not a duplicate/non-issue — main agent should proceed
with the queued fix (wrap runTurn call in session.turn(), return an honest one-line error
answer, still call writeLog/writeSidecar for the failed turn). ADD to the fix scope: ensure
session.close() (or at minimum stream.end()/sidecar.end()) still runs on the caught-error
path so end-markers are written and streams are flushed — the try/catch alone (catching only
inside turn()) does not guarantee that if the catch re-throws or if runChat itself is later
refactored; safest is a try/finally around the for-await loop body in runChat that always
calls session.close().
STATUS: ✅ DONE — commit 9593c1a, both the session.turn() try/catch and the runChat
try/finally landed exactly as recommended; verified manually via a temporary forced-throw
patch (reverted before commit), 1033/1033 tests green.

